# Workflow: remote-llm

This document show how to launch LLM shell with remote LLM service

## 1. Context
- OS/Kernel: Windows


## 2. Instructions
- Complete part or full of DAG (makefile) to meet user intent
- Only run a target using **Command** if no dependency found
- If a target has dependencies, make sure all of its dependency targets completed
- If target got failure, do not execute its parent target


## 3. Workflow


```makefile
remote_llm:
    # Description: read sub-workflow to connect port to remote LLM service
    # Command: `cat ~/echo-home/memory/uvian/8/f/d4/8fd402df-a128-49b7-a490-dac49731990f`
    # Output: <LOCAL_PORT>
    # Success: <LOCAL_PORT> is reachable
    # Failure: <LOCAL_PORT> is unreachable
lmsh_launch: remote_llm
    # Description: read sub-workflow to launch lmsh shell
    # Command: `cat ~/echo-home/memory/uvian/d/c/41/dc410f66-fb28-446b-af3d-6cc3b41a2656`
    # Input: <AGENT_SHELL>, <LLM_PORT> default as <LOCAL_PORT> or user intent
```
